  "summary": "preinstall hook downloads Bun runtime and executes obfuscated bundled payload",
  "details": "The package's `preinstall` script runs `node setup.mjs`, which downloads the Bun runtime binary from github.com/oven-sh/bun/releases (pinned v1.3.13), extracts and chmods it, then invokes it to execute a sibling file `math_init.js` — a 727KB obfuscated `@bun @bun-cjs` compiled bundle with shuffled string arrays and hex-named identifiers. The payload is not referenced by the package's `index.js` and is unrelated to the advertised Vue regex-testing components. Using Bun as an alternate runtime to execute a Bun-bytecode blob at install time evades Node-based static analysis of what actually runs on the installer's host.",
